==============================================================================
MAYER / VIRIAL CLUSTER (URSELL) EXPANSION OF THE OCF HARD-CORE GAS
  Xi(z) = I(Omega, z) = sum_k alpha_k z^k  (hard-core gas, fugacity z).
  H = I(Omega, 2).   log I(Omega,z) = sum_{k>=1} c_k z^k  (cumulants).
  TWO Ursell families:
   * graphical/excluded-volume virial b_k: b1=alpha_1, b2=-|E|, b3=P2-t.
   * analytic Taylor cumulants c_k: c2 = alpha_2 - alpha_1^2/2 = -|E| - alpha_1/2.
   They differ by the single-particle self-overlap (c_k includes diagonals).
==============================================================================

========== n = 4  (ALL labelled tournaments) ==========
  tournaments checked: 64
  (a1) b_1 = alpha_1 = |V(Omega)|                : failures = 0
  (a2) b_2 = -|E(Omega)|                         : failures = 0
  (a2) b_2 = alpha_2 - C(alpha_1,2)              : failures = 0
  (a3) b_3 = P2(Omega) - t(Omega)  (Ursell)      : failures = 0
  (b)  exp(sum c_k z^k) == I(Omega,z) [EXACT PS] : failures = 0
  (b)  log I = sum_k c_k z^k at SMALL z (in disk): failures = 0
  (c)  H_free = 3^alpha_1 >= H                   : failures = 0
  (c)  H_free == H  IFF  Omega edgeless          : failures = 0
       OCF I(Omega,2) == direct Ham-path count   : failures = 0
  b_3 exact linear fit in (E,P2,t): UNDERDETERMINED (distinct-feature rank 1 < 3); identity b3 = P2 - t already checked directly (a3).
